  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">DEC Ukraine Humanitarian Appeal DePaul International</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Partner: Depaul Ukraine

Funding source: DEC appeal

Total number of direct beneficiaries (individuals): 31,043

Contect: Depaul Ukraine will build on their existing expertise and reach in Ukraine to provide food assistance and social services to some of the 6.5 million IDPs created by the conflict in Ukraine.

Key activities: scale up purchasing of food and refining logistics to distribute supplies to soup kitchens, outreach to home of vulnerable people and families &amp; distribution points run by DePaul staff and volunteers. 75 individuals to receive permanent shelter or supported accommodation for six months. Welfare checks for vulnerable adults and families. Supported accommodation for homeless single mothers and their children. Operating an orphanage for children with complex disabilities in Ivano-Frankivsk region. Capacity strengthening of local staff in humanitarian response (including security, safeguarding, humanitarian standards, programme quality &amp; implementation, logistics and procurement)

Activity split:
90%: Food, nutrition &amp; livelihoods in emergencies
10%: Water, sanitation &amp; hygiene in emergencies</narrative>
  </description>
